{
"dur": 74.053,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 7.767,
"text": "Here's the difference that changed everything. A normal processor is like one very smart worker doing tasks one after another, very fast.",
"end": 8.042
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 8.042,
"vo_start": 8.317,
"vo_end": 13.991,
"text": "A GPU is like thousands of simple workers, each doing one small calculation at the same time.",
"end": 14.266
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 14.266,
"vo_start": 14.541,
"vo_end": 25.298,
"text": "For graphics, that's perfect: every pixel can be worked on at once. But lots of other problems look the same. Weather. Chemistry. Physics.",
"end": 25.573
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 25.573,
"vo_start": 25.848,
"vo_end": 32.088,
"text": "In 2006 Nvidia announced CUDA, software that let scientists program its graphics chips for any kind of calculation.",
"end": 32.363
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 32.363,
"vo_start": 32.638,
"vo_end": 38.158,
"text": "It was expensive. Every chip had to carry extra hardware for it, and for years, hardly anyone paid for it.",
"end": 38.433
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 38.433,
"vo_start": 38.708,
"vo_end": 46.988,
"text": "Wall Street didn't like it. Nvidia's share price fell hard after 2008. Jensen kept funding CUDA anyway, and gave it to universities.",
"end": 47.263
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 47.263,
"vo_start": 47.538,
"vo_end": 57.451,
"text": "In 2008 things got worse. A manufacturing defect in some laptop chips forced Nvidia to set aside about two hundred million dollars, and the financial crisis hit at the same time.",
"end": 57.726
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 57.726,
"vo_start": 58.001,
"vo_end": 67.401,
"text": "From its 2007 peak, the stock lost more than three quarters of its value. Investors asked why Nvidia was spending so much on a product almost nobody used.",
"end": 67.676
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 67.676,
"vo_start": 67.951,
"vo_end": 73.103,
"text": "He was betting that somewhere, some researcher would find a job only this kind of chip could do.",
"end": 74.053
}
],
